.TH CCREPO 1 "2026-07-22" "atelier instruments" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccrepo \- Claude Code usage totals, grouped and filtered any way you like
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccrepo
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ccrepo
.BI \-g " list"
.RI [ filters ]
.RI [ \-\-sort
.IR list ]
.br
.B ccrepo
.RB [ \-\-json | \-\-csv | \-\-flat ]
.RB [ \-\-fx
.IR code ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccrepo
totals what Claude Code has cost you and lets you slice that total along any
dimension the logs record \(em by repository, model, git branch, main thread
versus subagent, entrypoint, Claude Code version, agent type, or any calendar
bucket from year down to hour \(em nested however you ask.
.PP
It reads Claude Code's raw session logs under
.I ~/.claude/projects/
directly and computes cost itself,
.BR "per message" ,
from a local price table. Working at the single-message grain is the whole
point: it is what lets
.B ccrepo
group by dimensions that vary
.I within
a session \(em the branch a message was sent from, whether it came from the main
thread or a subagent, which Claude Code version wrote it \(em not just the
coarse repo/model/day totals a per-session tool can offer.
.PP
Cost here is an API-equivalent
.BR estimate :
what the usage would bill at Anthropic's public list prices, not what your
subscription actually charges. For a plan holder the two differ, and the
.B BILLING
section below explains the optional
.I Actual
column that reconciles them.
.SS How cost is computed
Each message carries five classes of token \(em input, output, cache read, and
a cache write split into 5-minute and 1-hour tiers.
.B ccrepo
prices each class from a built-in per-model table (USD per million input
tokens, keyed by the short model name via longest-prefix match) and the four
standard multipliers Anthropic applies to the other classes. The table is a
dated snapshot; a machine-local
.I ~/.claude/ccrepo-pricing.json
overrides or extends it without touching the tool. See
.B COST AND RECONCILIATION
below.
.SS ccusage as the oracle
.B ccrepo
computes its own cost, but it does not ask you to trust that blindly. On every
run it also invokes
.BR ccusage (1)
and reconciles its own grand total against ccusage's, reporting the drift in
both dollars and percent as a footnote under the table. ccusage is the
.IR oracle :
when the two agree the local price table is current; when they diverge the
footnote says so, per model, so a stale price announces itself instead of
lying quietly. The cross-check is skippable for a faster or offline run \(em see
.BR \-\-no\-reconcile .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Grouping
.TP
.BI \-g " list" "\fR, \fP" \-\-group " list"
An ordered, comma-separated list of dimensions, nested left to right. Valid
dimensions are
.IR repo ", " model ", " branch ", " kind " (main | subagent), "
.IR entrypoint ", " cc\-version ", " agent ", " year ", " month ", " week ", "
.IR day " and " hour .
The default is
.IR repo .
Use
.I total
(or an empty list) for a single grand total with no breakdown. For example
.I \-g repo,model
totals each repo and breaks it down by model;
.I \-g model,repo
inverts that nesting. An unknown dimension is refused.
.SS Filtering
Each filter takes a comma-separated list. Within one filter a comma means OR; a
leading
.B !
on a term excludes it; a
.B *
globs; matching is case-insensitive. Across different filters the conditions
combine with AND. Most dimensions match exactly, with two conveniences:
.B \-\-model
matches as a substring and
.B \-\-session
matches as a UUID prefix.
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " list"
Restrict to repositories, e.g.
.I \-\-repo ros,faves
or
.IR "\-\-repo '!scanme'" .
.TP
.BI \-\-model " list"
Restrict to models by substring, e.g.
.IR "\-\-model opus" .
.TP
.BI \-\-branch " list"
Restrict to git branches, e.g.
.IR "\-\-branch 'client\-*'" .
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " list"
Restrict to
.I main
or
.I subagent
messages.
.TP
.BI \-\-entrypoint " list"
Restrict to an entrypoint, e.g.
.I cli
or
.IR claude\-vscode .
.TP
.BI \-\-cc\-version " list"
Restrict to a Claude Code version, e.g.
.IR 2.1.209 .
.TP
.BI \-\-agent " list"
Restrict to an agent type.
.TP
.BI \-\-session " list"
Restrict to sessions by UUID prefix, e.g.
.IR "\-\-session 01c3,ff97" .
.TP
.BI \-\-since " YYYYMMDD"
Include only messages on or after this local date.
.TP
.BI \-\-until " YYYYMMDD"
Include only messages on or before this local date.
.TP
.BI \-z " tz" "\fR, \fP" \-\-timezone " tz"
Passed through to
.BR ccusage (1)
for the reconciliation cross-check, so both sides bucket dates in the same zone.
.SS Sorting
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " list"
A per-level sort, aligned position-for-position to
.BR \-g ;
a single value broadcasts to every level. Each entry is a key, optionally
suffixed
.BI : dir
.RB ( asc " or " desc ).
Keys are
.IR cost ", " tokens ", " count " (distinct sessions), " name " and " time .
The default is chronological for time dimensions and cost-descending for
everything else. An unknown key or direction is refused.
.SS Output format
.TP
.B \-\-flat
Emit one column per group level (a spreadsheet shape) instead of the default
indented tree with subtotals.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit tidy JSON: a
.I meta
block plus one record per leaf, each dimension its own field. Mutually
exclusive with
.BR \-\-csv .
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Emit the same tidy shape as CSV. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-json .
.SS Currency
.TP
.BI \-\-fx " code"
Convert all amounts to an ISO-4217 currency, fetched live. The default is
.IR nzd ;
pass
.I usd
for the raw list-price figures with no conversion. A non-USD currency needs
network access to fetch the rate.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " n"
Force the USD-to-target rate instead of fetching it (useful offline). Has no
effect on USD figures, and must be positive.
.SS Reconciliation and billing
.TP
.B \-\-no\-reconcile
Skip the
.BR ccusage (1)
cross-check. Faster, and works offline, at the cost of leaving the local total
unchecked against the oracle.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-billing
Ignore
.I ~/.claude/ccrepo-billing.json
and report the estimate only, even when a plan config is present.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise usage digest and exit. This manual is the full reference.
.SH COST AND RECONCILIATION
The built-in price table records, per model, the USD list price per million
.I input
tokens. The other four token classes derive from that base by Anthropic's
standard multipliers \(em output at 5\(mu, cache read at 0.1\(mu, a 5-minute
cache write at 1.25\(mu and a 1-hour cache write at 2\(mu \(em so one base
number prices all five classes. Model names match by longest prefix, so a dated
model id such as
.I haiku\-4\-5\-20251001
resolves to the
.I haiku\-4\-5
base. A model absent from the table is counted at
.B $0
and flagged, never silently guessed.
.PP
The table is a snapshot, checked against ccusage's own per-model cost on real
logs at the time it was taken. Because list prices move, every run reconciles
.BR ccrepo 's
grand total against
.BR ccusage (1)
and prints the drift. The reconciliation footnote reads out mine-versus-ccusage
totals, the delta in dollars and percent over the matched sessions, the largest
per-model divergences, and any sessions seen by only one side (a scope or
pruning difference). A large or growing drift is the signal to refresh the price
table \(em drop an updated
.I ~/.claude/ccrepo-pricing.json
or edit the built-in snapshot. Because ccusage cannot honour
.BR ccrepo 's
non-date filters, the cross-check is computed over the date-comparable scope,
not the fully filtered display set.
.SH BILLING
By default every figure is an API-equivalent estimate at list prices. A
machine-local
.I ~/.claude/ccrepo-billing.json
plan config adds an
.I Actual
column alongside the estimate: tokens on a plan-covered model cost
.B $0
marginal, and the flat monthly plan fee is apportioned across usage \(em by
covered-token share where there is covered usage in range, otherwise by
total-token share \(em plus any uncovered per-token spend. The config names the
plan, its monthly cost, which model families it covers, and any per-token
carve-outs. Absent, or suppressed with
.BR \-\-no\-billing ,
.B ccrepo
reports the estimate only. The plan fee shown is one month; over a multi-month
range the true outlay is (months \(mu fee). The billing model is described in
full in
.I instruments/README.md
in the atelier repository.
.SS Actual spend versus the estimate
The
.I Actual
column reprices usage under the plan, but it does not on its own answer the
money question: over the whole range, is what you
.I genuinely pay
more or less than the API list price would have been? An optional
.I spend
block in the billing config supplies the genuine outlay and
.B ccrepo
reconciles it against its own estimate \(em the money-side analog of the ccusage
cross-check \(em in a footnote that reads out billed versus estimate, the delta
in dollars and percent, and the months it spans. Two modes:
.B plan
(the default) takes billed as the plan fee times the distinct months in scope,
plus any uncovered per-token spend \(em making the
.RI ( months " \(mu " fee )
outlay observable and reconciled;
.B usage
sums an invoiced or metered figure you record per month, so a metered or
tier-changing bill is exact. A month with no recorded figure is reported as a
gap, never smeared into the delta, and a range the config cannot answer for
degrades to a stated
.I unavailable
line rather than a guessed number. Like the ccusage cross-check the comparison
is computed over the whole date-comparable scope, not a dimension-filtered
slice \(em the subscription fee is global, so comparing a per-repo estimate
against the whole plan fee would be apples-to-oranges. The
.I spend
schema and worked examples are in
.I instruments/README.md
in the atelier repository.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/
The source: Claude Code's raw session logs, read read-only. A repo's true name
is recovered from the
.I cwd
recorded inside each log, not from the dash-mangled folder name.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/ccrepo-pricing.json
Optional local price overrides, merged over the built-in table. Malformed JSON
is ignored with a warning, never fatal.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/ccrepo-billing.json
Optional plan config that enables the
.I Actual
column and, via an optional
.I spend
block, the actual-spend-versus-estimate reconciliation. Malformed or missing a
positive
.I plan.monthlyCost
\(em ignored with a warning; a bad
.I spend.mode
falls back to plan mode and a malformed period entry is dropped, never fatal.
Holds a person's plan and real spend, so it stays machine-local and never enters
a repository.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ccrepo
Per-repo totals in NZD (the default).
.TP
.B ccrepo \-g month
Totals per calendar month.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-g repo,model
Each repo, broken down by model.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-g model,repo
Each model, broken down by repo.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-g repo,branch \-\-repo ros
Just the
.I ros
repo, broken down by branch.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-g kind
Main-thread spend versus subagent spend.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-g repo \-\-sort name
Repos listed alphabetically instead of by cost.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-\-fx usd \-\-no\-reconcile
Raw list-price figures, offline, with no ccusage cross-check.
.TP
.B ccrepo \-\-json > usage.json
Tidy JSON for scripting.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
.PP
.B 2
on a usage error \(em an unknown
.B \-g
dimension, an unknown or badly-directed
.B \-\-sort
key,
.B \-\-json
and
.B \-\-csv
together,
.B \-\-rate
on USD figures where it has no effect, or a non-positive
.BR \-\-rate .
.PP
.B 1
on a runtime failure \(em notably a currency conversion whose rate could not be
fetched (offline, with no
.B \-\-rate
override), or any unexpected error.
.SH NOTES
Cost is an API-equivalent estimate at list prices, not your subscription bill;
the
.I Actual
column reprices it under a plan, and the
.I spend
block (see
.BR BILLING )
reconciles it against what you genuinely pay. Neither is fetched from a billing
API \(em there is none \(em so both are only as true as the machine-local
config.
.PP
Calendar buckets (day, hour, week, and the
.BR \-\-since / \-\-until
filters) use
.I local
time on purpose \(em a day means the local one. Currency defaults to NZD and is
converted live, so a plain run needs network access both for the conversion and
for the
.BR ccusage (1)
cross-check;
.B \-\-fx usd
and
.B \-\-no\-reconcile
together make the run fully offline. No personal path is baked into the tool:
the source, price and billing locations are all derived from the home directory
at runtime.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ccusage (1),
.BR ccarchive (1),
.BR cctranscript (1),
.BR jq (1)
.PP
The instruments overview, including the billing model:
.I instruments/README.md
in the atelier repository.
